> Subject: FOIA Request — DTC Tokenization Services No-Action Letter, December 11, 2025
>
> Pursuant to the Freedom of Information Act, 5 USC 552, I request records concerning the Division of Trading and Markets’ December 11, 2025 no-action response titled “No-Action Letter Request Related to The Depository Trust Company’s Development of the DTCC Tokenization Services.”
>
> I request the complete administrative and staff work-product file associated with this no-action matter, including records maintained as formal public guidance or staff interpretations and the associated supporting documentation and background materials.
>
> In particular, this request includes:
>
> 1. Internal analyses and work product, including substantive drafts of the no-action response, draft language, memoranda, legal analyses, work papers, notes, briefing materials, issue papers, recommendations, and comments or edits made during review.
> 2. Approval, concurrence, and routing records, including sign-off sheets, routing slips, approval records, supervisory comments, internal recommendations, and records identifying the persons or offices that reviewed, concurred in, approved, or authorized issuance of the response.
> 3. Records concerning whether the matter was presented or referred to the Commission, Chair, or any Commissioner, including any action memoranda, seriatim memoranda, vote sheets, voting records, Commission Action System records, Office of the Secretary records, or other records reflecting Commission consideration, if any.
> 4. Communications concerning the request, including substantive communications among Division of Trading and Markets staff and communications with the Office of the Chair, Commissioners or their staffs, Office of General Counsel, Office of the Secretary, other SEC divisions or offices, DTC, DTCC, or their representatives.
> 5. Meeting records, including meeting requests, agendas, notes, minutes, summaries, presentations, attachments, and other materials concerning meetings or calls regarding the requested no-action relief.
> 6. Internal tracking and matter-management records, including the matter or request number, database or log entries, status histories, assignments, workflow records, and other metadata identifying how the request was received, assigned, reviewed, approved, and closed.
> 7. Records addressing the decision to provide no-action relief concerning Section 19(b) of the Exchange Act and Rule 19b-4, including analysis of whether DTC's proposed Tokenization Services otherwise would require a proposed rule change under Section 19(b) or Rule 19b-4.
>
> This request is intended to encompass records maintained by the Division of Trading and Markets, including the Office of Clearance and Settlement, and records of Jeffrey S. Mooney, Elizabeth Fitzgerald, the Division Director, and any other personnel assigned to or substantively involved in the matter. It also encompasses responsive records concerning this matter located in the Office of General Counsel, Office of the Secretary, Office of the Chair, or Commissioners’ offices.
>
> For purposes of identifying the relevant records series, NARA disposition authority DAA-0266-2019-0005-0001 expressly encompasses formal public guidance and staff interpretations, including no-action-letter requests, and DAA-0266-2019-0005-0003 expressly encompasses:
>
> > “Internal background and supporting records used to prepare interpretations and No-Action Letters, including, but not limited to, substantive drafts, work papers, and internal memorandum.”
>
> I cite these disposition authorities to assist the Commission in locating the requested records; I am not limiting this request only to records formally classified under those authorities.
>
> The relevant public no-action response is dated December 11, 2025. The incoming request was addressed to Jeffrey Mooney, Associate Director, Office of Clearance and Settlement, Division of Trading and Markets. The SEC response was likewise dated December 11, 2025.
